@* EVT-3 Ticket 3 (owner verbatim, EVENT-TIMEPLACE-1: "At the top, right
   below the header of the 'event' frontier, I want Time: and Place: ...
   They're both explorable elements."): ONE reusable frontier-metadata row
   -- an OPTIONAL small-caps LABEL beside one or more explorable VALUE
   chips the caller composes. Reusable anywhere a frontier carries
   time/place facts (the owner's own composability bar: "any kind bearing
   them composes them") -- NOT Event-only markup; any future capability-bearing
   kind (IHasTimeAndPlace) reaches this the same way
   EventDateAndPlacesSection does, never a second hand-rolled row.

   EVT-META-TOP-1 (fix round 2, owner verbatim: "we don't need to have
   TIME: and PLACE:. just put the actual values; AD 31 and Galilee...");
   amended verbatim: "have the time and place next to each other; not
   stacked."): `Label` is now OPTIONAL (`null` renders no label span at
   all -- bare values only) -- STILL a genuinely reusable knob, not
   deleted: a future consumer that DOES want a label can still supply one.
   EventDateAndPlacesSection now composes exactly ONE row (Label omitted)
   whose own ChildContent holds BOTH the time value AND every place value
   as sibling chips in the SAME flex row -- "next to each other" falls out
   of that composition directly, not a second layout mode here. *@
<div class="popover-frontier-metadata-row" data-testid="@TestId">
    @if (Label is not null)
    {
        <span class="popover-frontier-metadata-label">@Label</span>
    }
    <span class="popover-frontier-metadata-values">@ChildContent</span>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; }
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string TestId { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = default!;
}
